Xiv?†alphaxiv.org )\nL96: \nL97: [Input] Links to Code Toggle\nL98: \nL99: CatalyzeX Code Finder for Papers (cite35†What is CatalyzeX?†www.catalyzex.com )\nL100: \nL101: [Input] DagsHub Toggle\nL102: \nL103: DagsHub (cite36†What is DagsHub?†dagshub.com )\nL104: \nL105: [Input] GotitPub Toggle\nL106: \nL107: Gotit.pub (cite37†What is GotitPub?†gotit.pub )\nL108: \nL109: [Input] Huggingface Toggle\nL110: \nL111: Hugging Face (cite38†What is Huggingface?†huggingface.co )\nL112: \nL113: [Input] ScienceCast Toggle\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2511.09101] Ultra-Light Test-Time Adaptation for Vision--Language Models (https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.09101)\nciteturn5973view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.09101\",\"lineno\":8}); Total lines: 166\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 12 Nov 2025]\nL9: # Title:Ultra-Light Test-Time Adaptation for Vision--Language Models\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Byunghyun Kim L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Ultra-Light Test-Time Adaptation for Vision--Language Models, by Byunghyun Kim\nL14: \nL15: cite6†View PDF cite7†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:Vision-Language Models (VLMs) such as CLIP achieve strong zero-shot recognition by comparing image embeddings to text-derived class prototypes. However, under domain shift, they suffer from feature drift, class-prior mismatch, and severe miscalibration. Existing test-time adaptation (TTA) methods often require backpropagation through large backbones, covariance estimation, or heavy memory/state, which is problematic for streaming and edge scenarios.\nL17: We propose Ultra-Light Test-Time Adaptation (UL-TTA), a fully training-free and backprop-free framework that freezes the backbone and adapts only logit-level parameters: class prototypes, class priors, and temperature. UL-TTA performs an online EM-style procedure with (i) selective sample filtering to use only confident predictions, (ii) closed-form Bayesian updates for prototypes and priors anchored by text and Dirichlet priors, (iii) decoupled temperatures for prediction vs.\nL18: calibration, and (iv) lightweight guards (norm clipping, prior KL constraints, smoothed temperature) to prevent drift in long streams.\nL19: Across large-scale cross-domain and OOD benchmarks (PACS, Office-Home, DomainNet, Terra Incognita, ImageNet-R/A/V2/Sketch; ~726K test samples) and strong TTA baselines including Tent, T3A, CoTTA, SAR, Tip-Adapter, and FreeTTA, UL-TTA consistently improves top-1 accuracy (e.g., +4.7 points over zero-shot CLIP on average) while reducing ECE by 20-30%, with less than 8% latency overhead. Long-stream experiments up to 200K samples show no collapse.\nL20: Our results demonstrate that logit-level Bayesian adaptation is sufficient to obtain state-of-the-art accuracy-calibration trade-offs for VLMs under domain shift, without updating any backbone parameters.\nL21: Comments:  | 7 pages\nL22: Subjects:  | Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (cs.CV)\nL23: Cite as:  | cite8†arXiv:2511.09101 [cs.CV]\nL24:    | (or cite9†arXiv:2511.09101v1 [cs.CV] for this version)\nL25:    | cite10†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2511.09101†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL26: ## Submission history\nL27: \nL28: From: Byunghyun Kim [cite11†view email ]\nL29: [v1] Wed, 12 Nov 2025 08:19:57 UTC (13 KB)\nL30: \nL31: Full-text links:\nL32: \nL33: ## Access Paper:\nL34: \nL35: View a PDF of the paper titled Ultra-Light Test-Time Adaptation for Vision--Language Models, by Byunghyun Kim\nL36: \nL37:   * cite6†View PDF L38:   * cite7†HTML 