ce (cite32†What is Huggingface?†huggingface.co )\nL117: \nL118: [Input] ScienceCast Toggle\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2511.09286] Enriching Knowledge Distillation with Cross-Modal Teacher Fusion (https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.09286)\nciteturn5973view4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.09286\",\"lineno\":8}); Total lines: 161\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 12 Nov 2025]\nL9: # Title:Enriching Knowledge Distillation with Cross-Modal Teacher Fusion\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Amir M. Mansourian , cite6†Amir Mohammad Babaei , cite7†Shohreh Kasaei L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Enriching Knowledge Distillation with Cross-Modal Teacher Fusion, by Amir M. Mansourian and 2 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite8†View PDF cite9†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:Multi-teacher knowledge distillation (KD), a more effective technique than traditional single-teacher methods, transfers knowledge from expert teachers to a compact student model using logit or feature matching. However, most existing approaches lack knowledge diversity, as they rely solely on unimodal visual information, overlooking the potential of cross-modal representations.\nL17: In this work, we explore the use of CLIP's vision-language knowledge as a complementary source of supervision for KD, an area that remains largely underexplored. We propose a simple yet effective framework that fuses the logits and features of a conventional teacher with those from CLIP. By incorporating CLIP's multi-prompt textual guidance, the fused supervision captures both dataset-specific and semantically enriched visual cues.\nL18: Beyond accuracy, analysis shows that the fused teacher yields more confident and reliable predictions, significantly increasing confident-correct cases while reducing confidently wrong ones. Moreover, fusion with CLIP refines the entire logit distribution, producing semantically meaningful probabilities for non-target classes, thereby improving inter-class consistency and distillation quality.\nL19: Despite its simplicity, the proposed method, Enriching Knowledge Distillation (RichKD), consistently outperforms most existing baselines across multiple benchmarks and exhibits stronger robustness under distribution shifts and input corruptions.\nL20: Comments:  | 11 pages, 5 figures, 8 tables\nL21: Subjects:  | Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (cs.CV)\nL22: Cite as:  | cite10†arXiv:2511.09286 [cs.CV]\nL23:    | (or cite11†arXiv:2511.09286v1 [cs.CV] for this version)\nL24:    | cite12†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2511.09286†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL25: ## Submission history\nL26: \nL27: From: Amir Mohammad Mansourian [cite13†view email ]\nL28: [v1] Wed, 12 Nov 2025 12:50:15 UTC (5,534 KB)\nL29: \nL30: Full-text links:\nL31: \nL32: ## Access Paper:\nL33: \nL34: View a PDF of the paper titled Enriching Knowledge Distillation with Cross-Modal Teacher Fusion, by Amir M. Mansourian and 2 other authors\nL35: \nL36:   * cite8†View PDF L37:   * cite9†HTML (experimental) L38:   * cite14†TeX Source L39: \nL40: cite15†view license†creativecommons.org L41: ### Current browse context:\nL42: \nL43: cs.CV\nL44: \nL45: cite16†< prev |   cite17†next > L46: \nL47: cite18†new | cite19†recent | cite20†2025-11 L48: \nL49: Change to browse by:\nL50: \nL51: cite21†cs L52: \nL53: ### References & Citations\nL54: \nL55:   * cite22†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L56:   * cite23†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L57:   * cite24†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.